# graphify corpus exclusions (gitignore syntax)
#
# graphify's built-in SKIP_DIRS covers node_modules/.git/dist/build/coverage,
# but deliberately allows dot-dirs ("users often want .github/, .claude/").
# That is right for skills and agents and badly wrong for worktrees.

# Agent worktrees are FULL COPIES of this repo created by isolated agent
# sessions. Indexing them made the codebase appear ~4x over: the graph reached
# 378MB with 474,152 references to worktrees/agent-*, which distorts god nodes,
# community detection and every query that leans on them.
#
# Excluded from the graph only — never delete these from disk (see CLAUDE.md:
# "worktree-agent-* branches ... never delete from here").
.claude/worktrees/

# Everything else under .claude/ is kept on purpose: skills/, agents/, rules/
# and workflows/ are hand-authored and genuinely part of how this project works.

# Frozen planning archive + its screenshot/vision-review JSON artifacts.
# Superseded by vault/ (see CLAUDE.md) and pure generated noise.
.planning/**/screenshots/

# Local scratch + build artefacts that carry no architecture.
.next/
graphify-out/

# Throwaway QA capture dirs. These are per-run screenshot artefacts, not
# architecture, and vision extraction over ~1,300 of them is pure cost.
.qa-tmp-*/
docs/screenshots/
public/screenshots/
audit-verify-*.png
editor-*.png
edit-*.png
